{
  "simplified_explanation": "As a high school student, Tim Costello asked his teacher if poverty is just a natural part of life. He later decided it isn’t—poverty happens because of human decisions and policies. Now 69, he has spent more than 30 years fighting poverty in Australia and around the world. He’s been to war and disaster zones, served as mayor of St Kilda, written books, and been named a national living treasure. People sometimes mix him up with his brother, Peter Costello, who was Australia’s treasurer. Tim Costello is well known as a Baptist minister and for leading the charity World Vision for 13 years."
}

